{
  "_readme": [
    "WATCHDOG VALUATION CALIBRATION  \u00b7  SOUTH JERSEY",
    "",
    "Every municipality in the seven South Jersey counties, all starting at 1.00.",
    "1.00 means no adjustment, so uploading this file as-is changes nothing. It is",
    "here so you never have to remember the exact spelling of a town key.",
    "",
    "HOW TO SET ONE, from a closing you actually know:",
    "",
    "      factor = actual sale price / what this page estimated",
    "",
    "  The page said $292,000 for a home in Woodbury Heights and it closed at",
    "  $357,500.  357500 / 292000 = 1.22.  So you change that town's line to:",
    "",
    "      \"WOODBURY HEIGHTS BORO (GLOUCESTER)\": 1.22",
    "",
    "  Use three or four known closings per town and average the factors. One",
    "  house being off is the house, not the town. Re-check a couple times a year.",
    "",
    "READ THIS BEFORE YOU START ADJUSTING:",
    "  The page now measures a live ratio from recent recorded sales in each town,",
    "  which already corrects for market drift and stale assessments on its own.",
    "  Calibration is a thumb on the scale for what is left over. Reach for it only",
    "  when a town is consistently off in the SAME direction across several sales",
    "  you can verify. If you find yourself editing most of these, something else",
    "  is wrong and the fix belongs in the model, not in this file.",
    "",
    "  Check the diagnostics panel first. Add ?debug=1 to any lookup URL and it",
    "  shows whether the estimate came from a live measured ratio or fell back to",
    "  the published one. A town falling back is the more likely culprit.",
    "",
    "RULES:",
    "  Allowed range is 0.50 to 2.00. Anything outside that is ignored.",
    "  Keys are county qualified because WASHINGTON TWP and GREENWICH TWP each",
    "  exist in two South Jersey counties. Do not shorten them.",
    "  '_default' below applies to any town with no entry of its own. Leave it at",
    "  1.00 unless you have evidence the whole model leans one way.",
    "",
    "COVERAGE: 168 municipalities.  Atlantic 23,  Burlington 40,  Camden 36,  Cape May 16,  Cumberland 14,  Gloucester 24,  Salem 15"
  ],
